<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kursk</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kursk is a city in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seym-river">Seym</a> river, first mentioned in 1032. It was a town of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chernigov">Chernigov</a> lands on the edge of the steppe and was destroyed in the Mongol invasion of 1240. Muscovy refounded it as a frontier fortress in 1586. In 1943 the region around it saw the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kursk">Battle of Kursk</a>, one of the largest tank battles in history.</p></div>
